(5894777, 856152, 30049, '<td valign="top">Hey! Wait a second here...Chit?!  I totally missed that.  &lt;blush&gt;  :-)<br/> <br/>I was looking over some of the comments I made recently and took another peek at your photo.  The Chit reference just hit me...</td>', 'Hey! Wait a second here...Chit?!  I totally missed that.  <blush>  :-) I was looking over some of the comments I made recently and took another peek at your photo.  The Chit reference just hit me...', '2010-03-08 12:07:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5894787, 855869, 105457, '<td valign="top">Hi Nitin, greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Regarding your photo:<br/> <br/>Composition<br/>The image flows very well, I really like the bokeh on the background.<br/>The way the petals are just hanging over the bottom of the image is very peaceful and tranquil.<br/> <br/>Technique<br/>I imagine it must be hard to get all in focus at f/5.6, you were probably on the long end of your lens? Maybe some ISO could be sacrificed in order to get a smaller aperture and get everything in focus.<br/> <br/>Processing<br/>Just as a lot of people said, the tones are so vibrant, and the colour rendition is very good.<br/>Lovely whites and yellows.<br/> <br/>Processing<br/>Effective, very low profile but it did the trick.<br/> <br/>Overall, I think you were downvoted because of the flower issue. Although it''s not just a flower, it becomes a great part of the subject matter. The winner is also a macro but without flowers, so I guess that you could have scored higher if it was all in focus and you didn''t have such a big flower in your shot.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=105457" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">contact me</a>.<br/>Regards,<br/>Joao</td>', 'Hi Nitin, greetings from the Critique Club! Regarding your photo: CompositionThe image flows very well, I really like the bokeh on the background.The way the petals are just hanging over the bottom of the image is very peaceful and tranquil. TechniqueI imagine it must be hard to get all in focus at f/5.6, you were probably on the long end of your lens? Maybe some ISO could be sacrificed in order to get a smaller aperture and get everything in focus. ProcessingJust as a lot of people said, the tones are so vibrant, and the colour rendition is very good.Lovely whites and yellows. ProcessingEffective, very low profile but it did the trick. Overall, I think you were downvoted because of the flower issue. Although it''s not just a flower, it becomes a great part of the subject matter. The winner is also a macro but without flowers, so I guess that you could have scored higher if it was all in focus and you didn''t have such a big flower in your shot. If you have any questions feel free to contact me.Regards,Joao', '2010-03-08 12:14:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5895228, 856117, 64568, '<td valign="top">Really great shot Sara, my fav bird. We have one that comes at 7:30am and 4:30pm everyday for a feed-up. Saw a Redwing the other day, they like a raw carrot chopped a bit or apple. ;)</td>', 'Really great shot Sara, my fav bird. We have one that comes at 7:30am and 4:30pm everyday for a feed-up. Saw a Redwing the other day, they like a raw carrot chopped a bit or apple. ;)', '2010-03-08 16:47:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5896522, 855847, 44877, '<td valign="top">Hey Roz - so sorry I didn''t see this earlier. So caught up with my "stuff". HUGE congrats on another Blue!!! Those bugs are really working for you! I may go blind looking at them, but I''m happy to do it for you! OXOX ;oD</td>', 'Hey Roz - so sorry I didn''t see this earlier. So caught up with my "stuff". HUGE congrats on another Blue!!! Those bugs are really working for you! I may go blind looking at them, but I''m happy to do it for you! OXOX ;oD', '2010-03-09 12:30:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5897113, 855847, 108069, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 10 when I voted and commented that I couldn''t stop going back to it. I still can''t. A truly incredible photo. Congratulations on the well-deserved blue.</td>', 'I gave this a 10 when I voted and commented that I couldn''t stop going back to it. I still can''t. A truly incredible photo. Congratulations on the well-deserved blue.', '2010-03-09 18:20:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5901831, 855753, 112628, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. I would have loved to include more of the wheel and the box, but there were several plants just out of this shot that were obstructing my view of them. As it wasn''t my garden, I wasn''t exactly in a position to move the ornament or replant anything, lol.<br/> <br/>I kept the picture intentionally dark, as my first impression of the ornament was a fanciful notion of it coming to life at twilight and doing garden work on the sly. I agree that the beak needed to stand out more, but I couldn''t arrive at an edit I liked that brought out the beak while staying true to the other colours and elements.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I would have loved to include more of the wheel and the box, but there were several plants just out of this shot that were obstructing my view of them. As it wasn''t my garden, I wasn''t exactly in a position to move the ornament or replant anything, lol. I kept the picture intentionally dark, as my first impression of the ornament was a fanciful notion of it coming to life at twilight and doing garden work on the sly. I agree that the beak needed to stand out more, but I couldn''t arrive at an edit I liked that brought out the beak while staying true to the other colours and elements.', '2010-03-12 20:32:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5904220, 856318, 67697, '<td valign="top">that''s too bad this got such a lousy score.  this is awesome!  so funny.</td>', 'that''s too bad this got such a lousy score.  this is awesome!  so funny.', '2010-03-14 20:35:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5909520, 855934, 12796, '<td valign="top">you already know half the story here as already told by others - "better focus required"<br/>I guess you went too close to the subject for the camera to properly focus.<br/> <br/>The subject in my opinion again is not something where I would prefer a close up shot. Maybe yes if you had the option to cut and shoot indoor with no other distractions (like what you see as another stem with two other tomatoes I believe).<br/> <br/>I would have used the wide side of my lens and suitably changing the composition that I can find some less distracting elements. It would have been ok, if it was a bunch of tomatoes rather than just 2 but less interesting.<br/> <br/>I hope the above is taken in the right spirit. Keep shooting.<br/> <br/><i>Edit: darn typos</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-03-18 11:20:53.</i></td>', 'you already know half the story here as already told by others - "better focus required"I guess you went too close to the subject for the camera to properly focus. The subject in my opinion again is not something where I would prefer a close up shot. Maybe yes if you had the option to cut and shoot indoor with no other distractions (like what you see as another stem with two other tomatoes I believe). I would have used the wide side of my lens and suitably changing the composition that I can find some less distracting elements. It would have been ok, if it was a bunch of tomatoes rather than just 2 but less interesting. I hope the above is taken in the right spirit. Keep shooting. Edit: darn typos', '2010-03-18 11:02:39.000000', '2010-03-18 11:20:53.000000', 0),
(5910927, 854804, 12796, '<td valign="top">you have a very interesting subject in this photo. Fortunately you didn''t commit the mistake which I did by not taking a photograph of a flower. However, in spite of the subject being terrific, this photo scored below 4.5<br/> <br/><b>Couple of reasons why I believe:<br/></b>It is difficult to understand what exactly is your main subject. Is it the ant/group of ants in their habitat or is it the flower which has been converted into a nest by the ants. Furthermore the DOF is shallow and hence not diluting your background from interfering on your subject.</td>', 'you have a very interesting subject in this photo. Fortunately you didn''t commit the mistake which I did by not taking a photograph of a flower. However, in spite of the subject being terrific, this photo scored below 4.5 Couple of reasons why I believe:It is difficult to understand what exactly is your main subject. Is it the ant/group of ants in their habitat or is it the flower which has been converted into a nest by the ants. Furthermore the DOF is shallow and hence not diluting your background from interfering on your subject.', '2010-03-20 07:03:03.000000', NULL, 0),
